    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 acceptance tests green).\n\n## What I changed\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete, and the create-time duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners. I kept structural impact low by routing both behaviours through the **service layer** rather than touching the large controller or the many small policy classes.\n\n**5 files:**\n\n1. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 the two behavioural edits, both in trivial (CC\u22481) methods:\n   - `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted=true` and `save`s (retains the row) instead of `delete`.\n   - `findAllOwners` filters out deleted owners: `...findAll().stream().filter(o -> !o.isDeleted()).toList()`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `deleted` column field + `isDeleted`/`setDeleted` (defaults `false` for new owners).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` (and thus the JSON response) exposes it; MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column and seeded existing owners `FALSE` (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`; the default h2 profile auto-updates its schema).\n\n## Why this satisfies the spec cheaply\n\nThe create endpoint's blocking check (`OwnerHouseholdPolicy`, plus the identity/possible-duplicate policies) all iterate `clinicService.findAllOwners()`. Filtering deleted owners at that single source makes every one of those checks ignore deleted owners \u2014 so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted \u2014 without editing the controller, any policy, or growing any function. `GET` still uses `findOwnerById` (unfiltered), so a deleted owner is still returned with `deleted: true`.",
